{{fbdoc item="title" value="Compiler Option: -edebuginfo"}}----
Add debug information

{{fbdoc item="syntax"}}##
	**-edebuginfo**
##
{{fbdoc item="desc"}}
	The ##**-edebuginfo**## compiler inserts debugging symbols into output files, to use with GDB-compatible debuggers.

	C debug output preserves named parameters and automatic local storage and writes without duplicate native unused-storage diagnostics for analyzed bodies. Opaque assembly retains conservative behavior. Source unread-parameter and unread-variable warnings keep their normal behavior; optimized values can still be unavailable to the debugger. See ##[[CompilerOptg|-g]]##.

	With the C backends, private source entries retained solely for debugging also retain native code in optimized objects. Unused compiler-generated default members and internal read-only implementations still follow ordinary reachability. See ##[[CompilerOptg|-g]]##.
	
	##**-edebuginfo**## is automatically implied by the ##[[CompilerOptg|-g]]## option.
	
	##[[KeyPgDdfberr|__FB_ERR__]]## can be used to determine in user source code if the ##**-edebuginfo**## option was specified or implied on the command line.

{{fbdoc item="ver"}}
	- Since fbc 1.07.0

